Native-rate audio clips skip the sinc resampler

Carve plays audio clips through WaveNodeRealTime with libsamplerate's sinc
converter (EngineSetup.h: ClipDefaults), because the default path --
WaveNode and its Lagrange interpolator -- re-derives its ratio from a whole
number of source frames each block, so a file at another rate than the
engine wobbles in time by up to half a sample: sidebands at -37dB around a
1kHz tone, and a top octave rolled off by 2-5dB.

The sinc converter is built whatever the two rates are, though, and at a
ratio of exactly 1 it still low-passes (-3dB at ~21.2kHz for 44.1kHz), so a
file already at the output rate came out no longer bit-identical to itself.
Lagrange at a ratio of exactly 1 is a pure copy, latency-compensated, so a
file at the output rate takes that reader instead. Speed changes ride on the
reader's speed ratio rather than on the rates, and Carve's clips have none;
a time-stretched clip keeps the reader it asked for.

diff --git a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_WaveNode.cpp b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_WaveNode.cpp
index 2f76477..7e1aa2d 100644
--- a/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_WaveNode.cpp
+++ b/modules/tracktion_engine/playback/graph/tracktion_WaveNode.cpp
@@ -2113,7 +2113,11 @@ bool WaveNodeRealTime::buildAudioReaderGraph()
     const bool timestretchDisabled = timeStretcherMode == TimeStretcher::Mode::disabled;
     std::unique_ptr<ResamplerReader> resamplerAudioReader;
 
-    if (resamplingQuality == ResamplingQuality::lagrange)
+    // A file already at the output rate needs no conversion, and the sinc
+    // converters would still band-limit it (to ~21kHz at 44.1kHz). Lagrange
+    // at a ratio of exactly 1 passes the samples through untouched.
+    if (resamplingQuality == ResamplingQuality::lagrange
+         || (timestretchDisabled && loopReader->getSampleRate() == outputSampleRate))
         resamplerAudioReader    = std::make_unique<LagrangeResamplerReader> (std::move (loopReader), outputSampleRate);
     else
         resamplerAudioReader    = std::make_unique<HighQualityResamplerReader> (std::move (loopReader), outputSampleRate, resamplingQuality);
